.TH CTPOOL_FUTURE_CREATE_DETACHED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_future_create_detached \- create a standalone future with no pool or queued task
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ctpool_future *ctpool_future_create_detached(char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a future object that is not backed by any cthread_pool task
queue. An external producer (for example an event-driven engine that
is not itself a ctpool worker) is responsible for calling
ctpool_future_fulfill exactly once to deliver the result.

The returned future has a reference count of 2 on success, mirroring
ctpool_submit_future's convention: one reference held by the caller
(released via ctpool_future_free), one held by the producer (released
by ctpool_future_fulfill). The struct is freed once both sides have
released their reference, in either order; ctpool_future_free may
be called before ctpool_future_fulfill, exactly as with pool-backed
futures.

Always uses standard malloc/free, independent of any custom allocator
; matching ctpool_submit_future's existing futures, whose lifetime
is deliberately decoupled from any single allocator.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
err_str   Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
          (pass NULL to ignore)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a new ctpool_future handle (not yet done) on success.
Returns NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_future_fulfill (3),
.BR ctpool_future_get (3),
.BR ctpool_future_done (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
